6. Calls for urgent and extended humanitarian pauses and corridors throughout the Gaza Strip for a sufficient number of days, respected by all parties, to enable the full, rapid, safe and unhindered humanitarian access of United Nations humanitarian agencies and their implementing partners, the International Committee of the Red Cross and other impartial humanitarian organizations, in accordance with the humanitarian principles of humanity, impartiality, neutrality and independence;
7. Demands that all parties allow, facilitate and enable the immediate delivery of humanitarian assistance to civilians throughout the Gaza Strip, including through all available crossings and without preconditions, including food, water, fuel, medical supplies, electricity and emergency repairs to essential infrastructure, and ensure the safe movement of aid convoys, medical evacuations and civilians, and calls for the opening of all crossings and the lifting of restrictions on the movement of humanitarian personnel and supplies so that assistance can reach all areas, including northern Gaza;
8. Demands that all parties refrain from using starvation as a method of warfare and ensure safe and unhindered access for humanitarian relief personnel and supplies;
9. Demands that all parties protect medical personnel, hospitals, medical facilities, schools, ambulances, United Nations personnel and premises, humanitarian workers and journalists, and refrain from attacks against them, in accordance with international humanitarian law, and calls for accountability for violations against them;
10. Underscores the importance of coordination, humanitarian notification and deconfliction mechanisms to protect all medical and humanitarian staff, vehicles including ambulances, humanitarian sites and critical infrastructure, including United Nations facilities, and to help facilitate the movement of aid convoys and patients, in particular sick and injured children and their caregivers;
11. Rejects forced displacement of the civilian population in the Gaza Strip, demands that all parties refrain from such acts, and calls for the safe return of displaced persons to their homes;
12. Calls for an immediate humanitarian ceasefire leading to a sustainable cessation of hostilities, and calls upon all parties to take urgent steps to create conditions for a sustainable cessation of hostilities, including through the implementation of extended humanitarian pauses and the immediate and unconditional release of all hostages; stresses that any sustainable cessation of hostilities must be respected by all parties and must not allow Hamas or other armed groups to rearm or replenish their military capabilities, and calls upon all parties to engage constructively in diplomatic efforts to this end;
13. Calls on all parties to refrain from actions that could lead to regional escalation, and calls for respect for the sovereignty and territorial integrity of all States in the region, including Lebanon and Syria, and condemns all violations thereof;
14. Reaffirms its unwavering commitment to the two-State solution based on the legitimate national rights of the Palestinian people, including the right to self-determination, with Israel and Palestine living side by side in peace and security within recognized borders, stresses the importance of unifying the Gaza Strip with the West Bank under a reformed and revitalized Palestinian Authority, and calls for renewed efforts to achieve a just, lasting and comprehensive peace;
15. Requests the Secretary-General to report orally to the Security Council within 10 days on the implementation of this resolution, and further requests the Secretary-General to identify options to effectively monitor the implementation of this resolution, including through a strengthened humanitarian notification and deconfliction mechanism, and to present options, as a matter of urgency, for establishing a United Nations monitoring and verification mechanism to monitor the implementation of this resolution and report to the Council;
16. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

